1. Introduction

Cybersecurity awareness refers to understanding digital threats and knowing how to protect personal information, devices, networks and online accounts from cyberattacks.
As individuals and organisations increasingly depend on digital technologies, cybercriminals continue to use different techniques to steal information, disrupt services and gain unauthorised access to computer systems.
Phishing, malware, social engineering and password attacks are examples of threats that can compromise digital security.
Cyber threats such as phishing, malware and unauthorised account access can expose sensitive information and disrupt normal activities. Individuals can reduce these risks by developing good security habits, recognising suspicious online activities and protecting their personal information (Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency, 2021; Merritt, 2022).

